

Additional music-files for the MUSIPOC program

Thanks to Berthold Daum for his great MUSIPOC, the brilliant music-writer
and editor for the PSION S3 and S3a.
I wrote some samples of folksongs, well-known songs and hymnes of many
countries on the MUSIPOC for the Series 3 in order to have the program
known better. I sometimes had a few troubles as not all the notes are
coming as clear as I wanted to have them, but, nevertheless, I think these
files can be loaded by other music-interested persons. You can load the
files, play them, hear them, you can also edit or amend them as you like.
I include two applications, HYMNE.ALS for the \HYMNEN\TUN\*.SND and
HYMNEN.ALS for the \HYMNEN\TUN\*.TUN for your guidance. I found it was
better to separate the hymnes from the other music files and, thus, I wrote
these ALIAS-applications. If you like you can load the files in this way.
The files are FREEWARE, I wrote them for fun. I also include the converted
files for the MUSIPOC for the Series 3a just for your fun. I hope you enjoy
the music. If yes, drop me a line when you like.

